# Wave W17-U (Route 203): coal pine — a mine-country pine in smoke-dulled greens, tiered and full, its crown dusted pale where the coal smoke settles on it, highlight lifted clear of the turf, on coal turf (ground baked in). Route 203’s own tree — split from Route 204’s bluff pine beside it by the dusted crown (mine smoke vs clean bluff air) and from Route 202’s broadleaf gate oak by form entire.
